                The production quality kept its extraordinary standards in this sequel, and maybe a bit more. But the writing felt stagnant to me and a bit confused and unable to present historical events in the funny, dramatic, interesting way as the prequel did. That being said, the writing was good in many aspects and coherent in general. The characters remained the strength of the show. Although more were introduced in this sequel, each was perfect and balanced in design and voice acting. <br />
<br />
I am starting to lose interest in the show since it’s clear that the writing quality will be worse and overwhelmed with how to
                  <span class="js-visible" style="margin-left: -4px;">...</span>
          <span class="js-hidden" style="display: none;">handle the historical war premise.</span>
