                A female villainess otome anime story with a twist in it: the story is told from the POV of the male character of interest, which is not the one reincarnated, but the FMC is.<br />
<br />
The story is beautiful and will surely make you smile like crazy and laugh at times, especially with that twist, as the FMC is a free spirited person that does whatever she wants, first thing being confessing that she&#039;s the villainess to the MC directly, which is quite the bold move ngl. The MC is the perfect prince type that can do whatever he puts his mind to, actually mastering everything that
                  <span class="js-visible" style="margin-left: -4px;">...</span>
          <span class="js-hidden" style="display: none;">he tries instantly, but this also is quite a problem as he became uninterested in most things in the world, so following him throughout the story feels unique, especially because he needs to deal with the antics of the FMC trying to adhere to the scenario of the game.<br />
<br />
While the POV of the MC is a strong plus in this story, I will also say that in my opinion it feels like a give and take for it, or at least in the anime, that is because we don&#039;t get to see that much of the FMC and her life in the story. This for me felt a bit like a problem, because I ended up wanting to see more of her and other characters that are gravitating near the FMC, but unfortunately, either because of anime time constraints or because they chose to, most of the things we get are from the MC&#039;s perspective and not from the FMC, which leads me to wanting to see more about the others as well, to be able to actually start caring about them better, and especially because they seemed interesting. From the comments on episodes though, especially towards the end, my understanding is that they cut out stuff that would bring more depth to the other characters, which is a shame, but they still adapted the main flow of the story, which is pretty nice overall. Might not have helped that at times, there were time skips, quite big ones at once, which might be from the original story, but it accentuated this feeling of missing parts.<br />
<br />
The main story is a pretty standard story in terms of events and such, so while the story does feel unique because of the different POV we are getting it from, in the end it is a pretty generic villainess story imho. It is well done though, even if it is the same stuff done already quite a lot, so if you like these types of anime, it will surely bring you satisfaction watching this show.<br />
<br />
Story: 8 -- Very interesting twist to have the story be told from the MC&#039;s view, but that also lead to the problem of feeling like parts of the story are missing, especially those that would build the other characters outside of the main cast<br />
<br />
Art: 8 -- Nice art, typical artstyle of otome anime<br />
<br />
Music: 8 -- Pretty good music<br />
<br />
Characters: 8 -- Good characters overall, pretty standard for otome stories, but man, I wish I could see more of certain characters... <br />
<br />
Enjoyment: 8 -- Enjoyed this anime, but it left me with a feeling that parts of the story are missing which I really wanted to see<br />
<br />
Overall: 8<br />
Right now it has 7.67 from 33.430 votes Ranked #1553 Popularity #2962 Members 73,754 as of 11/10/2026.<br />
I recommend this anime to people that enjoy villainess otome anime and want to see the twist of the story being told from the MC&#039;s viewpoint. <br />
The anime finished what felt like the main story, but there seems to be a sequel at the source material, although the anime doesn&#039;t feel like it needs one that badly. It was a satisfying end imho.</span>
              </div>
