                  <div class="thumb-right">
            <a href="https://myanimelist.net/anime/60543/Dandadan_2nd_Season" class="ga-click" data-ga-click-type="review-anime-title-pic">
              <img width="48" data-src="https://cdn.myanimelist.net/r/48x71/images/anime/1721/149001.jpg?s=0fe656c2fdfe712275033c34be1256cc" data-srcset="https://cdn.myanimelist.net/r/48x71/images/anime/1721/149001.jpg?s=0fe656c2fdfe712275033c34be1256cc 1x, https://cdn.myanimelist.net/r/96x142/images/anime/1721/149001.jpg?s=5d381866ba7c42315ecda3da608bc4b7 2x" class="lazyload" />
            </a>
          </div>
                I really enjoyed Dandadan Season 2, especially with how the author spread out the romance between Okarun and Momo throughout the season. Instead of rushing their relationship, we just keep getting these small moments here and there that leave you wanting more. Their scenes together in the van were probably my favorite. I was honestly squeeing like a girl during those moments because they were just so sweet.<br />
<br />
At the same time, those scenes also made me a little sad because I found myself feeling jealous of how cute their romance is. There is something about the way their relationship develops that feels very natural and
                  <span class="js-visible" style="margin-left: -4px;">...</span>
          <span class="js-hidden" style="display: none;">rewarding, especially because neither of them completely says what they feel yet. The season ending with Momo becoming extremely jealous after seeing the alien girl kiss Okarun was also a really fun cliffhanger. It immediately made me want to see what happens next, and I am already looking forward to the next season.<br />
<br />
The action was also excellent this season, especially everything involving Evil Eye Jiji. I really like the way Evil Eye fights. There is something about his movements, expressions, and especially the sound effects that makes him look incredibly cool and badass whenever he takes over.<br />
<br />
What I enjoyed even more was how difficult he was to deal with. Okarun, Momo, and everyone else had to resort to increasingly unconventional tactics just to contain him, and even after throwing basically every resource they had at the problem, they still could not completely defeat or get rid of him. I really like that kind of thing in action shows, where an enemy feels genuinely dangerous and the characters have to think creatively instead of simply becoming stronger and overpowering them.<br />
<br />
Season 2 managed to balance the supernatural action, comedy, and romance really well for me. The fights were exciting, Evil Eye was a great threat, and the slow progression between Okarun and Momo kept me emotionally invested the entire time. By the end, I was already desperate for more.</span>
              </div>
