              <img width="48" data-src="https://cdn.myanimelist.net/r/48x71/images/anime/1026/155965.jpg?s=cff0c7d42a7d3c7ec89848b3136db588" data-srcset="https://cdn.myanimelist.net/r/48x71/images/anime/1026/155965.jpg?s=cff0c7d42a7d3c7ec89848b3136db588 1x, https://cdn.myanimelist.net/r/96x142/images/anime/1026/155965.jpg?s=b2a63874fe3cde7af20e884a418ee704 2x" class="lazyload" />
            </a>
          </div>
                My feelings about this anime are a bit torn. There are definitely cute girls, and they are doing cute things, but that theme seems at odds with them being a group of engineers in college that are into drinking, philosophy, and vinyls. Visually the show is fantastic and it is a pretty cozy cgdct. If you&#039;re looking for something cute to kill some time then this will be a good watch. The fixation on alcohol just makes it feel a little weird. I understand having a theme, and wanting it to feel unique, it just misses the mark for me. Along with the alcoholism the
                  <span class="js-visible" style="margin-left: -4px;">...</span>
          <span class="js-hidden" style="display: none;">author ends up trying to do 3 things at once; showcasing alcohol, cute girls, and a bit of romance. It&#039;s too much hopping around without enough focus on one thing to really excel in a single 12 episode run. It simply wasn&#039;t satisfying.<br />
<br />
I appreciate some of the more visual and implicit story telling. It&#039;s nice when authors trust the reader to understand without saying every single thing. The main part that bugs me is the alcoholic theme combined with romance, there is just so much consistent use of alcohol that it feels wrong. It&#039;s also a weak choice for a gourmet given that half of the drinks showcased are beers, that our main cast proceed to skull so they can get sloshed as fast as possible. 5 tallboys, and they&#039;re picking up more on the way back?? All to go dip your feet into the river on a date?? Why did you get an odd number of drinks for 2 people? I&#039;m still annoyed about that. The other half are hard liquor on the rocks... I might not be the most interesting alcoholic in the world but even I think that&#039;s pretty weak when I think of gourmet shows like dungeon meshi or dagashi kashi showcasing their respective foodstuffs. No, reading a quote on a bottle of whiskey then saying it tastes woody doesn&#039;t count as gourmet.<br />
<br />
Like always, when you have a group of girls living together they have to all be lesbians. I enjoyed the chemistry between each of the couples, each with their own relatively unique dynamic and a bit of meaningful character exposition. I get that all that is the standard trope, I just think it&#039;s a lot trying to go over everything for 3 potential pairings in such a short amount of time. From all of the pairings the main couple&#039;s fixation on alcohol is much higher, which ends up feeling melancholy. Even when they&#039;re having a good time sober Ibuki pulls a couple of beers out of her pocket so they can get drunk immediately. Cute girls needing to be buzzed during 90% of their screen time to do cute things is not peak.</span>
              </div>
