                  <div class="thumb-right">
            <a href="https://myanimelist.net/anime/61316/Re_Zero_kara_Hajimeru_Isekai_Seikatsu_4th_Season" class="ga-click" data-ga-click-type="review-anime-title-pic">
              <img width="48" data-src="https://cdn.myanimelist.net/r/48x71/images/anime/1540/155824.jpg?s=8b79a8fcb6c0453a5edafbba461edceb" data-srcset="https://cdn.myanimelist.net/r/48x71/images/anime/1540/155824.jpg?s=8b79a8fcb6c0453a5edafbba461edceb 1x, https://cdn.myanimelist.net/r/96x142/images/anime/1540/155824.jpg?s=cf0b195997fd77d293e0e858b79f09ba 2x" class="lazyload" />
            </a>
          </div>
                I immensely enjoyed this season, especially during the failed loops involving amnesiac Subaru. The psychological horror, mysterious deaths, overwhelming enemies, and Subaru&#039;s gradual descent into madness were some of the most fascinating moments in the entire series for me. My enjoyment was easily at 9/10 during those episodes. I was particularly excited when amnesiac Subaru confidently declared his &quot;counterattack&quot; after suffering through so many horrific deaths. I genuinely thought he had figured out something extraordinary and was about to turn the seemingly impossible situation around through some clever, unconventional strategy.<br />
<br />
Unfortunately, my enjoyment declined after amnesiac Subaru merged with his original self. The story had spent
                  <span class="js-visible" style="margin-left: -4px;">...</span>
          <span class="js-hidden" style="display: none;">so much time establishing how ridiculously overwhelming the enemies were, making the situation feel almost impossible to overcome. Yet after Subaru recovered his memories, everything suddenly started falling into place. Julius managed to overcome Reid, Ram could suddenly overwhelm Lye with the help of Cor Leonis, and the other threats became much more manageable. I understand that there are explanations for these developments, but the shift still felt rather contrived. It was almost as if everyone received a plot armor buff the moment Subaru regained his memories.<br />
<br />
My biggest disappointment is that I expected a more unconventional resolution. I wanted amnesiac Subaru to figure out how to overcome these impossible odds through ingenuity, using everything he had learned from his repeated deaths. Instead, we got what felt like a fairly conventional series of heroic breakthroughs and victories. I don&#039;t mind the protagonists winning, but when the story establishes enemies as practically unstoppable, I want their eventual defeat to feel equally extraordinary without diminishing how threatening they were in the first place. The emotional developments were good, but they didn&#039;t completely make up for my disappointment with the narrative direction.<br />
<br />
Shaula was definitely one of the highlights of this season. Her backstory, personality, and tragic circumstances made her one of the most memorable characters in the Watchtower arc. I was disappointed, though, that Subaru couldn&#039;t even show her a little more affection during their farewell. I understand his loyalty to Emilia, but considering Shaula had waited 400 years for her master and was seemingly about to die, would it really have hurt him to give her some comforting words or affection? He certainly cried enough over losing her afterward. At least the little scorpion gives some hope that she isn&#039;t completely gone.<br />
<br />
As for Rem finally awakening, it was a nice cliffhanger, although it didn&#039;t particularly change my overall impression of the season. I can understand why that moment, along with the numerous emotional payoffs, would resonate strongly with many viewers.<br />
<br />
Overall, the writing is still good, and I genuinely enjoyed the season. I just wish the author had maintained the extraordinary tension and unpredictability of the failed loops all the way through the resolution. The buildup had me expecting something far more ingenious than what we eventually got. It&#039;s still a solid 8/10 for me, and despite my criticisms, I&#039;m definitely looking forward to the next season.</span>
              </div>
