                Well,<br />
I honestly did not expect to love Classroom of the Elite this much.<br />
When this Anime originally came out in 2017, I had basically zero interest in it. The synopsis did not catch me, the trailer did not catch me, and for years I simply ignored it. Now after finally giving it a chance, I can say that was a mistake. Season 1 is a straight-up Masterpiece for me.<br />
The biggest reason is obviously Kiyotaka Ayanokoji. At first he seems quiet, detached, almost boring on purpose. But the more the season continues, the more you realize that there is MUCH more happening inside his head. He observes
                  <span class="js-visible" style="margin-left: -4px;">...</span>
          <span class="js-hidden" style="display: none;">everything, calculates people, predicts reactions and manipulates situations without needing everyone to know that he was responsible.<br />
And THAT is what makes him so fascinating to me.<br />
He is not the typical protagonist who screams about friendship and wins because he believes hard enough. Ayanokoji treats situations almost like a chessboard. People have strengths, weaknesses, motivations and uses. Watching him quietly move everything into the position he wants was probably the biggest reason why I kept pressing &quot;next episode.&quot;<br />
I also really loved the philosophical quotes at the beginning of the episodes. Quotes from Western philosophers and thinkers might seem like a small detail, but they set the mood perfectly. Quite often you only understand why that particular quote was chosen after watching the episode.<br />
The special tests are another huge strength. On paper this is a school Anime, but it feels more like psychological warfare with grades attached to it. Alliances, betrayal, information, social pressure, manipulation — suddenly something as simple as a school exam becomes interesting.<br />
And then comes the ending.<br />
Without going deeply into spoilers: Ayanokoji&#039;s final inner monologue completely sealed the deal for me. It basically strips away any comfortable interpretation you might still have had of him and shows you how he REALLY views the people around him. That was the exact moment where I thought: yep, I need to continue this immediately.<br />
The animation is solid, the atmosphere works, and the soundtrack supports the psychological tone very well. But for me this Anime lives and dies with its characters and strategy.<br />
Season 1 introduced one of the most interesting protagonists I have seen in quite some time. Cold, calculating, manipulative and incredibly difficult to read.<br />
I went into Classroom of the Elite expecting basically nothing.<br />
I came out wanting Season 2 immediately.<br />
WATCH IT.</span>
              </div>
