                It&#039;s a movie that certainly has all it needs to be popular: great visuals, memorable soundtracks (especially the Eve songs, I love them!) and a cast of likeable characters that make you feel like you&#039;re alongside them, sharing the same pains and joys together. And perhaps the most importantly, a duo of main characters you can&#039;t help but root for not only romantically, which I must add I did not particularly care for, but also as people who are striding through life with struggles of their own. <br />
<br />
Grand depictions of nature as it is and how small we humans are in comparison, be it through
                  <span class="js-visible" style="margin-left: -4px;">...</span>
          <span class="js-hidden" style="display: none;">the eyes of Tsuneo as he dives deep into the embrace of the ocean, or be through the main question this movie constantly asks us at any given moment, whether or not we are prepared to fight for our dreams, ideals, through roads that are nothing but easy fills me with such deep appreciation of life, and the nature all around us. I cannot help but think of it as a fairytale, filled with so much extraordinary that it looks like a different world yet in which lies the true essense of humanity as we are. I think being able to create that appreciation of our position against the nature, whether we accept or reject it, try to change it or give our dreams to the waves that are ready to take it all away, is what&#039;s truly beautiful about this story.<br />
<br />
So yes, I do indeed recommend this movie to everyone, I wouldn&#039;t say it is a masterpiece, but feelingswise it is sure damn close to being there.</span>
              </div>
