      <div title="10:01 AM" class="update_at">Oct 11, 2026</div><div class="username">
          <a href="https://myanimelist.net/profile/AshParth" class="ga-click" data-ga-click-type="review-anime-reviewer">AshParth</a>
          </div><div class="tags"><div class="tag recommended btn-label js-btn-label" data-id="1" data-href="https://myanimelist.net/anime/57779/Dorohedoro_Season_2/reviews"><i class="fas fa-star"></i>Recommended</div></div>      <div class="text">
                  <div class="thumb-right">
            <a href="https://myanimelist.net/anime/57779/Dorohedoro_Season_2" class="ga-click" data-ga-click-type="review-anime-title-pic">
              <img width="48" data-src="https://cdn.myanimelist.net/r/48x71/images/anime/1603/155354.jpg?s=d43c950763d275b293e53937d396b5a1" data-srcset="https://cdn.myanimelist.net/r/48x71/images/anime/1603/155354.jpg?s=d43c950763d275b293e53937d396b5a1 1x, https://cdn.myanimelist.net/r/96x142/images/anime/1603/155354.jpg?s=ac85a3addf7a3d1fd539661af1b39d30 2x" class="lazyload" />
            </a>
          </div>
                Diving back into a world of chaos with Kaiman and Nikaido.  This is Dorohedoro once again.  So, as a reminder what I&#039;d thought about the previous season and the OVA before jumping into this.  The first season was a near-masterpiece and the OVA was a chill episode with a collection of six-short bonus chapters from the manga.  What does this season uphold?  A lot going on with old and new characters that converge into one gnarly finale that&#039;s set up for the next season.  Kaiman and Nikaido are traveling through the World of Sorcerers up until Mastema where they
                  <span class="js-visible" style="margin-left: -4px;">...</span>
          <span class="js-hidden" style="display: none;">meet a young woman named Natsuki, voiced by Sara Matsumoto (Japanese) and Anairis Quinones (English), who followed them because of Kaiman having Cross-Eye tattoos as she has one over one of her eyes.  She is willing to lead them to their hideout.  Meanwhile, we meet the Cross-Eyes gang that En thought he&#039;d got rid of except there are only a few of them that Risu, voiced by Soungdok (Japanese) and Alejandro Saab (English), who lived within Kaiman&#039;s esophagus and now is revived thanks to Kikurage and know who really killed him.  Before I continue, I didn&#039;t mention this character because Risu does pop up after being revived.  It was technically a spoiler.  I&#039;d also learned that in the English Dub, Billy Kametz voiced Risu before his unfortunate passing and Alejandro took over since 2022.  Rest in paradise, Billy.  Back on the topic of the Cross-Eyes, the remaining members consist of Dokuga, voiced by (Kouki Uchiyama (Japanese) and Kieran Regan (English), who can dress up like a moth, fly like one, and produce poisonous saliva; Ton, voiced by Katsuhito Nomura (Japanese) and Johnny Yong Bosch (English), who does knife tricks; Ushishimada, voiced by Atsushi Imaruoka (Japanese) and Christopher Swindle (English), who has super strength; Tetsujou, voiced by Daiki Kamano (Japanese) and Benjamin Diskin (English, who has lightning reflexes with a sword; and Saji, voiced by Tomokazu Koshimura (Japanese) and Bill Butts (English), who is the youngest of the group.  For the moment, the Cross-Eyes are making ends meet, living in this home owned by this landlady until they plan to usurp the En Family.<br />
As speaking of the En Family, they also have a lot going on such as Chota disguising himself as Nikaido since a Devil named Asu has had her escape from En&#039;s supervision until the gig is up.  Chota also finds a secret journal about Nikaido that involved her childhood, including an adopted family and her magic being the mythical time manipulation magic.  In addition, we learn that one of Nikaido&#039;s adoptive family members is still alive.  During a dream sequence En offers, Ebisu remembers that she had a family and travels to where they are located.  Shin and Noi travel meet up with Kasukabe, Jonson, Vaux and Thirteen to find the location of the Cross-Eyes with the help of Kasukabe&#039;s estranged wife, Haru.  However, it&#039;s not so easy when the conflict becomes brutal and complicated, especially when it comes to their leader.  I&#039;ve mentioned the past, and this anime does more than what it offers as we learn more about Kaiman&#039;s true identity.  Although, it is also complicated when Kaiman is suffering through major headaches as he remembers his past that is connected to Risu, who has a lot more on his plate, too.  Even more so when we make it to the finale when the tide of power turns between the Cross-Eyes and the En Family.  I won&#039;t spoil anymore than I&#039;ve already shared because the story goes a mindfuck.<br />
Yes.  It does sound like the story does go a little all over the place when we have multiple characters going out their way as well as we learn more about them.  However, that is the point.  We learn about these characters, especially Kaiman and Nokaido.  Keeping the themes of identity along with institutional trauma and the moral blur between factions.  What I&#039;d forgotten to mention in my review of the last season is that there are no signature protagonists or antagonists.  Sure, we have a division of class between humans, sorcerers and devils socially and politically.  No matter where you stand, life sucks.  You will have your fair share of friends and enemies.  En may be a narcissist at times when he does care for his family, but the Cross-Eyes have their share of blood in their hands even if they usurp En.  I would also agree that you might hate Kaiman for what he&#039;d transitioned to once he&#039;d learned about his true identity.  So, despite the story for every character going all over, their stories do converge into what the next season might be when someone else takes over the throne.  As a matter of fact, the characters are still pretty good with their own goals and their chemistry with one another.  Finding out about some of the other characters aside from Kaiman and Nikaido like Professor Kasukabe and his wife, Haru, and Ebisu with her family are entertaining in terms of character exploration.<br />
In the meantime, the animation itself continues to add the sort of mind numbing moments in the chaotic world of Dorohedoro.  The way the animation runs is much more improved when it comes to 3D modeled characters moving like 2D characters.  The character designs and the background are still amazing in terms of variety, exploring new places while retaining that dystopian charm.  It still has a butt load of gore and blood as the narrative goes.  The action is still as metal as it can be.  If I have to nitpick a little, it&#039;ll be when you see multiple healing factors come into play.  I know Dorohedoro takes place between the Hole, the World of Sorcerers and Hell, but it feels like the healing magic that is shown can be a bit of a copout at times.  But I digress.  It is Dorohedoro and like I&#039;ve said in the last season, you throw your morals out of the window while retaining some emotion like empathy, rage, and delight.  The voice cast, including  the new ones, are still amazing when I&#039;ve watched the show twice.  One in Japanese and one in English.<br />
Overall, like in the last season, this season is near-perfect as it started off casually after walking away from a chaotic finale back into some more chaos up to an even more gritty abrupt finale that&#039;s set up to what the third season will continue where it&#039;d left off.  Right after the conflict between one family to a faction they&#039;d thought was gone.  With even more chaos along with new places to explore, Hell isn&#039;t too far off since the anime is pretty much located right around the borders between the World of Sorcerer&#039;s and Hell.  It&#039;s also interesting to know that Devil Exams have more than what it was in the last season.  I&#039;ll give this chaotic second season eight bandaged Kaimans out of ten.  8/10.  Yes, I know this is like a point lower than the first season.  It&#039;s why this season is more chaotic than the previous season has been.  Where would the third season bring us?  Find out more.  This is Dorohedoro.</span>
