                  <div class="thumb-right">
            <a href="https://myanimelist.net/anime/61240/Futsutsuka_na_Akujo_dewa_Gozaimasu_ga__Suuguu_Chouso_Torikae_Den" class="ga-click" data-ga-click-type="review-anime-title-pic">
              <img width="48" data-src="https://cdn.myanimelist.net/r/48x71/images/anime/1958/158341.jpg?s=db31b169d1fbc0d0ff22edb16f90a423" data-srcset="https://cdn.myanimelist.net/r/48x71/images/anime/1958/158341.jpg?s=db31b169d1fbc0d0ff22edb16f90a423 1x, https://cdn.myanimelist.net/r/96x142/images/anime/1958/158341.jpg?s=ad246f3bfc048e68193975f686210852 2x" class="lazyload" />
            </a>
          </div>
                Though I Am an Inept Villainess is a charming, if ultimately overly simplistic take on the villainess subgenre. The narrative structure and general vibe of the character writing feels almost fairy tale-like, and while this does make for a vibrant and upbeat tone and compelling ensemble, a good deal of it feels a bit flat or lacking in depth, with the more outright antagonistic characters being too comically evil or mean-spirited in certain instances. The way that Reirin navigates being trapped inside the villainess’s body is generally very intriguing and did keep me interested in seeing how she would continue winning people over to her
                  <span class="js-visible" style="margin-left: -4px;">...</span>
          <span class="js-hidden" style="display: none;">side, but the fact that this experience doesn’t really change her outlook or perspective on anything dulls a good chunk of my interest.<br />
It is certainly a well-produced series on most fronts. Solid character designs are bolstered by rich color choices and the general competency and lack of jank you expect from a studio like Doga Kobo, and the timing of the comedic outbursts had me chuckling along more than I expected. I do wish that it had maybe reached for it a little harder though, as, despite its obvious polish, it also lacks anything particularly eye-grabbing. Overall, this is an exceptionally competent series, which is more than I can say about a lot of anime, but it’s also one that I’m probably going to forget about fairly quickly due to a distinct lack of substance both narratively and visually. The fact that I spent a good portion of my watch time thinking about how the actual villainess’s storyline was far more interesting certainly didn’t help, but I don&#039;t think I wasted my time either so I can still give it a decent recommendation.</span>
              </div>
