                Long story short: This season was mediocre at best, if not bad. <br />
<br />
-----<br />
<br />
Unfortunately, Clevatess 2nd season is one of those sequels that does not deliver the same of its prequel. <br />
<br />
1st season was fleshed out, with a nice pacing and good development even for secondary characters. You could feel that excitement and anxiety of &quot;what will happen next?&quot;, hoping everything will be &#039;daijobu&#039; and that they will overcome that tough situation.<br />
<br />
Now, the second season simply does not deliver any of that.....<br />
.<br />
                  <span class="js-visible" style="margin-left: -4px;">...</span>
          <span class="js-hidden" style="display: none;">.<br />
.<br />
It decided to be uninteresting, mediocre and... school. Yes, you read that right &quot;SCHOOL&quot;. Magic... is it the remake of Harry Potter already? I thought it would be released just in December this year. You start to wonder if it&#039;s the same anime you watching. <br />
<br />
Alicia does not shine as much. It&#039;s not Alicia&#039;s fault, it&#039;s just how mediocre the writing is. <br />
<br />
Every Alicia&#039;s &quot;deaths&quot; are basically ALL SAME. Every Alicia&#039;s struggle are basically same. This shows how lame and boring the writing is. <br />
<br />
You have random students that does not add nothing to the show. Nothing. And on top of that Nelluru has about 10 seconds of screen time the whole season. They add a bunch of random students but they put aside the most sweet and likeable character of the anime. <br />
<br />
The 2nd season drama is fully based on manipulation. Even a mirror or a piece of branch is ready and steady to manipulate or mind control the characters. Lame. Lame. Manipulation for the sake of plot device everywhere... everywhere. <br />
<br />
At its core, the story tries too hard to &#039;paper over the cracks&#039;. By the final episodes, you can guess why the Dark Beast of the North is doing what he&#039;s doing. But you know when they try to make it seem complex just to make it falsely intriguing? When in the end the root of it all is stupidly simple.<br />
<br />
For last: The flashbacks. Yes. Flashbacks are are hit or miss. But most of the times they&#039;ll be a miss. Flashbacks need that perfect timing; flashbacks can&#039;t spoil the mood nor interrupt the excitement, and they can&#039;t be much. Unfortunately, it&#039;s not what happens here. I would say there is at least 3 or 4 episodes of flashbacks that you could careless. <br />
<br />
I wish I could say something nice here, but unfortunately there isn&#039;t much. And I wish I could have enjoyed this season. Maybe I was harsh in this review exactly because I cared about the 1st season and so I was expecting the 2nd season to delivere same.<br />
<br />
<br />
-------<br />
<br />
If I could say something to my past self before watching this 2nd season, what would I say? <br />
&quot;Watch this second season only if a 3rd season is announced and/or if you deeply care for one of the characters. Otherwise, don&#039;t even bother&quot;.<br />
<br />
If a 3rd season ever happen, I&#039;ll watch it, but expecting it to be as good as the 1st season, otherwise I won&#039;t think twice before dropping =/</span>
              </div>
