                  <div class="thumb-right">
            <a href="https://myanimelist.net/anime/306/Abenobashi_Mahou☆Shoutengai" class="ga-click" data-ga-click-type="review-anime-title-pic">
              <img width="48" data-src="https://cdn.myanimelist.net/r/48x71/images/anime/1350/113655.jpg?s=9dd4e8329c4dc0cb5a912f3949015720" data-srcset="https://cdn.myanimelist.net/r/48x71/images/anime/1350/113655.jpg?s=9dd4e8329c4dc0cb5a912f3949015720 1x, https://cdn.myanimelist.net/r/96x142/images/anime/1350/113655.jpg?s=9d3e8ae56dfe89d9aee36abe9ae64e55 2x" class="lazyload" />
            </a>
          </div>
                Magical Shopping Arcade Abenobashi is a true masterpiece of anime. I had no idea at all what this was one was about and put it on one weekend as some background filler while I did some drawing … I didn’t draw a thing I just sat there and took this excellent anime in for all it’s worth.<br />
<br />
There are other reviews telling you all about the characters and the settings and the plot - so I just want to tell you how this show made me feel. This show took me on a ride that I did not expect at all and I am grateful for
                  <span class="js-visible" style="margin-left: -4px;">...</span>
          <span class="js-hidden" style="display: none;">it. The way it pokes fun at and parodies almost everything about anime is exactly the sort of thing I enjoy. Those who can step back and laugh at themselves and the things they love have a special power - and this show absolutely has that power locked down. <br />
<br />
 Anime fans will recognise tons and tons of references to other shows and genres - this entire show is paying respect to anime in general while also pointing a finger at how silly anime gets. I love this sort of thing - humour and action and hi-fiction all combined together to create something that just feels so damn good. This show was created in 2002 but it has that old school heart that older anime had - I can’t explain it in words - just some anime had a vibe that is almost unknown today - and when I find one of the shows that has that vibe I hold onto it dearly. I love to laugh - and Abenobashi makes me laugh a lot - like a LOT. <br />
<br />
 What really struck me about this show was how it goes from slap-stick madness and fan service to really emotional moments - and then back again. To be able to shift gears like that in a story like this takes something special and Abenobashi does it masterfully. The expressions in this show - the relentless savage critique of the genre - the way they handle the Pikachu knock off - it’s all solid gold. Pewy ?<br />
<br />
 An extremely well done anime that I would recommend to any and all fans of anime - and for those of us who’ve been around a bit and seen more than our fair share of anime this one has a little something extra in the sauce. I will absolutely be coming back to watch this one again and again for many years to come.</span>
              </div>
