                  <div class="thumb-right">
            <a href="https://myanimelist.net/anime/18679/Kill_la_Kill" class="ga-click" data-ga-click-type="review-anime-title-pic">
              <img width="48" data-src="https://cdn.myanimelist.net/r/48x71/images/anime/1464/111943.jpg?s=572ed6b737195bfa2660e1417805681b" data-srcset="https://cdn.myanimelist.net/r/48x71/images/anime/1464/111943.jpg?s=572ed6b737195bfa2660e1417805681b 1x, https://cdn.myanimelist.net/r/96x142/images/anime/1464/111943.jpg?s=bc85c6fbd60bedbcf790252f59c16b8f 2x" class="lazyload" />
            </a>
          </div>
                Kill la Kill is a great example of what anime can be when you put some heart and soul into it. I’ve been watching anime since the 80’s and without question Kill la Kill is among the best of the best of the best. Yeah it can take a second to get past the raging fan service and the tiny tight outfits - but at the same time this entire show is taking those overused tropes and making them the story - and our hero isn’t some generic dude  - it’s a girl out for revenge who is just as pissed off about the
                  <span class="js-visible" style="margin-left: -4px;">...</span>
          <span class="js-hidden" style="display: none;">silly outfits as all the haters. This show takes many of the tropes that anime haters hate on the most and rides them in for the win. <br />
<br />
 What seems like a cut and dry story wound up being way more than I expected. For a show as frantic and fast paced as this one it still manages to generate several moments that make you stop and think about what just happened and why. I wont drop any spoilers here so I’ll just say that most viewers will start this show on one side of a fence or the other - and by the end of it Kill la Kill does a great job of blowing that fence away entirely. <br />
<br />
To be honest I didn’t sit down to write a review for this show at all - I really just want to talk about Mako Mankanshoku. After re-watching this show for the third time I must proclaim Mako Mankanshoku as my all time favourite anime character , bar none. Her undying energy , her undying faith in her friends , her undying willingness to sacrifice herself , her undying love for her family , her undying belief in herself and her willingness to act selflessly from the beginning right through to the very end all qualify her as the goat. The way they animate her scenes of encouragement - the way she affects everyone in the story with her blazing positivity and her unwillingness to give up - I can’t really think of any other character that even comes close to being as amazing as Mako.  This show has an S level cast and for Mako to stick out among them is a true testament to the awesomeness of her character. <br />
<br />
 I strongly recommend this show to all fans of anime. Yes there’s an almost cringe level amount of groin snapping costume changes and underboob in this show but that’s actually part of the story and if you get it you get it - if you don’t then you won’t and that’s fine. The animation , the characters , the setting and even the way it all ends are excellent. I could really deep dive into this show but I see other reviewers has already taken care of that - so I shall wrap this up with the one thing that has stuck with me after watching this show for the 3rd time … <br />
<br />
<br />
Mako Mankanshoku forever.</span>
              </div>
