                After watching every Konosuba anime adaptation, I saved this one for last, and it was worth it, both as a farewell until season 4 and as a timekiller, of sorts.<br />
Being basically what konosuba has been all the way, there were still some things that I&#039;ve liked in here that were looked over in the main series, such as the whole deal with the Crimson Demon Village, who turned out to be way cooler folks than I thought, also some more screen time for Megumin&#039;s sister, Komekko. Knowing where it&#039;ll all lead made all encounters look much more exciting to me, seeing how Megumin&#039;s life completely
                  <span class="js-visible" style="margin-left: -4px;">...</span>
