          </div><div class="tags"><div class="tag recommended btn-label js-btn-label" data-id="1" data-href="https://myanimelist.net/anime/42310/Cyberpunk__Edgerunners/reviews"><i class="fas fa-star"></i>Recommended</div></div>      <div class="text">
                  <div class="thumb-right">
            <a href="https://myanimelist.net/anime/42310/Cyberpunk__Edgerunners" class="ga-click" data-ga-click-type="review-anime-title-pic">
              <img width="48" data-src="https://cdn.myanimelist.net/r/48x71/images/anime/1818/126435.jpg?s=a142eb20ff64d8a7629934284271b988" data-srcset="https://cdn.myanimelist.net/r/48x71/images/anime/1818/126435.jpg?s=a142eb20ff64d8a7629934284271b988 1x, https://cdn.myanimelist.net/r/96x142/images/anime/1818/126435.jpg?s=cdcc64c142f741a98c7d1f36ce899f5a 2x" class="lazyload" />
            </a>
          </div>
                I can’t express how awe struck I am with this show, everything from the writing, to the direction, both of art and the action sequences, to the MUSIC DIRECTION (arguably the best part) is just done so masterfully, with so much love, thought, efforts and care put into them<br />
<br />
Starting off with the overall setting and atmosphere, its so beautifully tragic, everything in night city represents the peak of how a hyper-capitalistic world and city would look like, with corporations fighting over tech/economic and social power to rule and expand their operations, no matter the cost borne, as long as it doesn’t overpower the profits, nothing
                  <span class="js-visible" style="margin-left: -4px;">...</span>
          <span class="js-hidden" style="display: none;">matters, Their cruel and clever nature are at the very epicenter of Night city and kick off the story as a whole, Everyone is selfish, everyone is cruel, trust is a valuable asset, sharing which with the wrong person may lead to destruction and death<br />
<br />
Coming to the start of the story, Man is it great, David and his mother represent the common everyday family, they don’t have a lot of money or resources, yet they still work hard to keep things afloat, specifically David’s mom in this case, willing to give up everything if it means her son could have a better life than hers, Which only makes the events that succeed more impactful and tragic, we get to see glimpses of how this world treats those who don’t have a lot of monetary or social importance, both of which can only be gained in this world through exploitation, of people, or resources, of markets.<br />
<br />
Moving onto the main characters, they’re so incredibly human despite being cyborgs, and that’s the greatest accolade I can bestow upon them, They may seem cruel on the surface, but that’s the bare minimum that is needed if they wish to survive in Night City, They represent camaraderie, fraternity, love and it’s really refreshing to see how in this city of mega capitalistic soul-less corporations, Our crew represents they few remaining individuals that are human, Maine (the initial leader of the crew) and his guidance to David, Rebecca and her brother and their sheer madness and loyalty, and Lucy and the romantic tension between her and David are just great to witness, these dynamics are what keep the story engaging, and are well developed enough to emotionally impact the viewer when something affects our crew, They represent us, they aren’t the mega rich, they are just trying to make a living at best, and everyday is a gamble,<br />
<br />
From here I believe the most important and impactful elements of the show must be discussed, Ambition, Dreams, Family, and Life as whole, Lucy’s dream and how central it is to the plot is revealed much later on, though its omnipresence throughout and how it shapes the dynamics between her and David Is just so fascinating to witness. I won’t spoil much but I was just devastated by how melancholic the story becomes, yet still being so packed with action. the actions which David has to take, the emotional toll on him due to his actions, his brain and identity not being able to grasp the sheer volatility and pace through which his life is moving through, Him kind of becoming everything he hated, Him feeling alone, with each action being selfish and selfless at the same time, and at the end him partaking in something he knows for a fact he won’t be able to back down from due to all of this emotional burden and the way the story unfolds, all of this was something which explored beautifully in such a short span of time<br />
<br />
The antagonists are so well written in every aspect of the definition of well written, they’re witty, cruel, apathetic, chasing only and only self satisfying profits, destroying everything and everyone who dares step in between, Especially Faraday, yet somehow their actions don’t feel without a purpose, it is exactly because their actions have a purpose and are so deplorable that the antagonists become so frightening.<br />
<br />
The show does something wonderful and that is not speaking much and instead showing us, it’s evident everywhere from the characters’ faces to the destruction caused to the actions taken. The Show SHOWS more than it tells and when it does tell we all cry in unison, That’s how masterful writing is done<br />
<br />
If you want clinical depression mixed with witnessing some of the best creative direction, music, storyline, a progression which flows like Butter where nothing feels rushed, paired with a story that is more expressive and emotionally impactful, all of this in 10 eps, just go for it, no second thoughts, Edge-runners does a lot of things in 10 eps which major shows can’t accomplish even a 100. It&#039;s the kind of masterpiece you don’t get to witness very often, Loved it&lt;3</span>
              </div>
