                Smoking Behind the Supermarket with You is an anime, particularly for those who are somewhat or well into their careers, that will feel relatable and leave you with a sense of hope. It gives perspective that even when things feel gloomy and the job, hours, or life suck, you can still find moments that brighten up the day. The little things still matter and make a difference, and you can find those moments anywhere.<br />
<br />
The story is slow-moving, has no major plot points or progression, and the characters are not that deep—but that is what makes it good and drives the message home. <br />
<br />
Sasaki is a
                  <span class="js-visible" style="margin-left: -4px;">...</span>
          <span class="js-hidden" style="display: none;">salaryman who works a demanding job, leaving him to feel lonely because he doesn&#039;t have much time for his personal life. Tayama/Yamada is a young adult who works as a cashier at the supermarket Saskai goes to. Despite it not being the most interesting or fulfilling role, she still loves what she does. <br />
<br />
Together they break up the mundane parts of life and enjoy eachother&#039;s company and conversation over a cigarette. Over time, they develop a deep friendship (or perhaps more?) and help each other grow as they work through the tough moments of life. <br />
<br />
The artwork is also good and helps show the characters&#039; emotions very well. This is a great watch if you&#039;re looking for a slice of life that you can actually see yourself in, or could see someone else in.</span>
              </div>
