                This anime is weird. It has the story and animation quality to easily earn an 8/10, yet the way it presents itself brings my rating down to just under 7.5/10. Still, I don&#039;t understand its low MAL rating.<br />
<br />
The art and animation are both quite good, the action scenes are exciting, and the story is unique, even if it draws inspiration from a mix of other anime and manga. The MC and supporting could be more complex, but despite that the MC is quite fun to watch thanks to his personality and behavior.<br />
<br />
Two things hold it back for me:<br />
<br />
1. Sound design: The audio quality is weird
                  <span class="js-visible" style="margin-left: -4px;">...</span>
          <span class="js-hidden" style="display: none;">and inconsistent. Both the Japanese and original dubs occasionally sound as if they were recorded in an amateur studio. The music doesn&#039;t always fit the scenes and sometimes cuts off abruptly. It&#039;s not a major issue for me however.<br />
<br />
2. Plot progression: It follows mainstream trends, yet the anime also seems to attempt something avant-garde—and doesn&#039;t quite pull it off. I&#039;ve seen it wrongly compared to *Solo Leveling* simply because the MC looks somewhat similar and both series feature a system, but the MCs and their respective systems have little in common. The anime&#039;s attempt to balance mainstream appeal with more experimental storytelling results in an inconsistent flow and some unclear details (maybe just plot holes). The fight in the final episode, for example, was visually stunning and exciting, but how it was fought didn&#039;t make much sense (I am vague to avoid spoilers).</span>
              </div>
