                After four seasons, I&#039;m honestly getting tired of Classroom of the Elite.<br />
<br />
Every season seems to follow the same formula: special exams, temporary alliances, attempts to expel students, and somehow, everything revolves around Ayanokoji.<br />
<br />
My biggest issue isn&#039;t that Ayanokoji is intelligent or powerful. It&#039;s that he rarely seems genuinely challenged. No matter how many people target him, he always comes out on top with barely any effort. At this point, the tension is almost nonexistent because I never believe he might actually lose.<br />
<br />
The supporting cast is another problem. So many characters have potential, yet their stories constantly circle back to Ayanokoji. I especially wish the female
                  <span class="js-visible" style="margin-left: -4px;">...</span>
          <span class="js-hidden" style="display: none;">characters had more independence instead of repeatedly becoming part of his romantic storyline.<br />
<br />
That said, the season wasn&#039;t entirely disappointing. The White Room developments were interesting, and I enjoyed Ryuuen&#039;s confrontation with Hosen.<br />
<br />
But the real highlight was Koenji. Watching him compete independently, outsmart his opponents, and ultimately win the island exam was genuinely satisfying. He&#039;s arrogant, but he actually backs up his confidence with results. I would love to see more focus on his character in future seasons.<br />
<br />
Overall, Season 4 felt repetitive and predictable. Classroom of the Elite has an interesting premise and plenty of promising characters, but it keeps relying on the same formula to prove how exceptional Ayanokoji is.<br />
<br />
I already know he&#039;s extraordinary. I just wish the story would give everyone else a chance to be interesting, too.</span>
              </div>
