            </a>
          </div>
                I have watched the 2014 korean &quot;Liar Game&quot; live action series and enjoyed it quite a bit. Of course I was happy to see the original manga getting finally an anime adaptation.... and got disappointed quite a lot.<br />
When watching the anime, I remembered most of the games in S1 and their outcomes already, so I focused instead on the characters and the differences. Since I don&#039;t remember every single detail of the live action, there were still some surprises left for me, as well as some new characters in the anime to enjoy.<br />
<br />
I don&#039;t know, why the live action worked so well for me at
                  <span class="js-visible" style="margin-left: -4px;">...</span>
          <span class="js-hidden" style="display: none;">the time, but when I watched the anime, it didn&#039;t feel right at all. Nao is still a very annoying character (I mean.. who is this naive??), although she makes some progress throughout S1. The games were still interesting, but their pacing felt off. Especially the smuggling game had too many episodes for my liking, that it got tedious to watch. The side characters are flat as wooden planks and follow basically the same pattern: Smug in the beginning, laughing maniacally in the middle, crying and begging in the end. <br />
It bothered me a lot, that nearly every opponent gets rescued, while Nao and Akiyama stay in the games. I get, why they are doing this, but it feels stiff and superficial to me. <br />
<br />
I really love shows like these normally. High stake games, psychological drama, intelligent characters exploiting rules and turn hopeless events around, etc. But somehow Liar Game didn&#039;t satisfy that. It had all the pieces, yet failed to place them to a full picture. I don&#039;t know, if the korean live action was actually that much better, since I don&#039;t remember everything after so long, but I remember, that it felt more tense and complete. I really wanted to love this adaptation and I wonder, if I would love it, if I hadn&#039;t seen the live action or if I would still miss some things. <br />
At this point, I&#039;m unsure, if I want to watch S2, when it comes out.</span>
              </div>
