                I didn’t really understand the appeal of *Steins;Gate* that much. *Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood* is often called a masterpiece, but in my opinion, it doesn’t quite live up to that reputation. The art style is good, and the story has potential, but the execution isn’t as strong as I expected. There are several parts where I felt bored.<br />
<br />
I have similar issues with anime like *High School DxD*, *The Testament of Sister New Devil*, and *Hunter x Hunter*. Fans might consider these anime masterpieces, but from an average viewer’s perspective, they don’t necessarily deserve that label. That’s why I’d rate them somewhere between 7 and 8.5 rather
                  <span class="js-visible" style="margin-left: -4px;">...</span>
          <span class="js-hidden" style="display: none;">than calling them masterpieces.</span>
